A||N||9||Sweeet86GT||Why hood vents?||||1||
Z||000000||Sweeet86GT||08-23-2001||04:52 PM||||I been kinda absorbing all this info on Fiero's.<BR>A question comes to mind on the talk on hood vents.<BR>Why and do they do any good?<P>------------------<BR>DAVE DIXON<BR>Bay City,MI||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-23-2001||04:59 PM||||dont think its any 'cooling' help' but it would help release pressure under the front to prevent lift at high speeds. Fieros tend to do that, lite in the front. Think some do it just for the cosmetics.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||05:02 PM||||If the vent is placed correctly it can do 2 things... vent warm air from the radiator & (primarily) vent out pressured air at high speeds-  Many Fieros I've driven (mine ocassionally) have one or both headlight covers fly open at high speed (105+) due to the force of the air coming in lifting the door- once open, the force of 100mph air holds the door open until you can slow down a little!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-23-2001||06:52 PM||||I have hood vents on mine. <BR>The engine stays cooler. Noticed when driving around neighborhoods (25-30MPH) or in stop and go traffic it works great. On the highway at higher speeds the front feels like it has less "float" and the temp gauge stays very steady. <BR>I would recommend doing the vents.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Tina||08-23-2001||11:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>I have hood vents on mine. <BR>The engine stays cooler. Noticed when driving around neighborhoods (25-30MPH) or in stop and go traffic it works great. On the highway at higher speeds the front feels like it has less "float" and the temp gauge stays very steady. <BR>I would recommend doing the vents.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What Oreif said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Only drawback I have found so far, are the fine scratches  by the vents.<BR>Noticed them a few weeks ago, and they are multiplying.<BR>Probably from a the dust and stuff that goes through the vents.<BR>Working on a hood mask now to solve that problem.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||08-24-2001||01:39 AM||||Why hood vents?<P>thats easy,  because they look cool.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/paragonvents1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/paragonvents1.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
